  "asked": "Headless build for Brett (AmberX-AXF worktree, branch claude/amberx-look-fix). Read CLAUDE.md + _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md + _claude/rules/RULES.md first (repo copies; axHub via mcp__axHub__call axhub.memory_read if you can). Opus, one session, no sub-agents. Brett said do it now; push to main when tests are green. Brett's screen recording (Oct 31 19:39, AmberX at https://amberx.amberxai.com, phone) shows 3 bugs: 1. AmberX ignores the shared look: its Approvals/hub screens render light and generic, not like the other apps. AmberX must read shared/settings/appearance.json (appearance@1, axHub data API GET /data/shared/settings/appearance.json + /data-events SSE) exactly like the console and axhub-web do, apply palette, theme and density, and follow live changes. Theme tokens only. 2. The \"Approval waiting\" popup in AmberX shows a broken-frame icon: axHub refuses framing from amberx.amberxai.com. Fix: in MossesX/axHub, make https://amberx.amberxai.com allowed by default for approvals and embed framing (AXHUB_APPROVALS_FRAME_ANCESTORS / AXHUB_EMBED_FRAME_ANCESTORS defaults or allow-list), keep https-only and the cookie-domain rule, add a test. AmberX side: if framing still fails, show a clear Open-on-hub button instead of a dead frame. 3. ntfy/phone pushes show raw JSON ({\"type\":\"veto\",\"phase\":\"warning\",...}) and fire repeatedly (\"dunk dunk dunk\"). In axHub (vinnie.ts / push code), send human text: title = reason.title, body = \"Runs in 30 s, tap to deny\" etc., with click URL to the approval page and Deny/Approve now actions. Warning push once per call, never repeated. Also check AmberX's own veto alarm or notifications do not re-fire on every poll; ring once per phase. Work: clone MossesX/axHub next to this worktree for the axHub part. Run each repo's tests (AXF web test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + lifecycle check; axHub pnpm test). Push to main in both repos. Git push auth (never print the token): T=$(grep -m1 '^GITHUB_TOKEN=' /opt/axf/.axf-console/secrets.env | cut -d= -f2- | tr -d '\"\\r '); git -c safe.directory='*' -c http.extraheader=\"AUTHORIZATION: basic $(printf 'x-access-token:%s' \"$T\" | base64 -w0)\" push origin HEAD:main (fetch+merge origin/main and retest first if main moved). After axHub main moves, Coolify redeploys it; AmberX web redeploys from main too. If an env var on Coolify still needs changing, add a systems-check banner item with Auto fix instead of asking Brett. Report in detailed style (thing touched, what was wrong, what changed) in _claude/builds/reports/amberx-look-fix.md.",
